# Phase 18 paginated timeout fixture determinism

- Recorded: 2026-10-25 00:22:16 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`
- Base revision: `e0257dbb54cbb67964e719fb81d572e74697523e`
- Pinned Java reference: RocketMQ client 5.5.1.

## Finding

GitHub Actions run 40143142994 failed during Maven `verify` in
`verify-java-producer-core-fixtures`. The Java fixture expected a page timeout
of 2345 ms while the invocation received 2344 ms. The pinned
`MQClientAPIImpl.getAllTopicConfig` and `getAllSubscriptionGroup` methods
recompute remaining time from `System.nanoTime()` for each page, so exact
millisecond observations depend on execution timing. The failure did not
involve a changed Rust API or production implementation.

## Resolution

- `ProducerCoreFixtures` records whether each paginated topic-config and
  subscription-group request has a positive remaining timeout budget instead
  of capturing the timing-dependent millisecond value.
- The fixture's configured input timeout remains exact. The delayed 20 ms
  timeout cases still verify that expiration prevents a later page request.
- `fixtures/producer/core.json` was regenerated. Changes are limited to the
  request timeout observations for the two paginated APIs.

## Verification

- `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml -Dproducer.core.fixture.verify=false verify` — PASS; regenerated the producer fixture.
- `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` — PASS in default fixture verification mode.
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --test admin_rpc get_all_topic_config_matches_java_pagination_and_version_fixtures --locked` — PASS (1 test).
- `git diff --check` — PASS.
- Current-head remote CI must run after this fix is pushed.

The four pre-existing Phase 19 worktree paths remained unchanged and unstaged.
